SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #4 - Weaverville Wander
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Rating:** Very Strenuous for Ste
 ep Elevation Gain\n**Distance:** 7 miles\n**Elevation:** 1\,100 feet\n**Su
 rface:** Road\n**Pace:** 3.2 mph\n**Gear:** 2L water\, snack\, poles for t
 he climb up Hamburg.\nFeatures: Get to know Weaverville\, Lake Louise\, an
 d views from the top. This route begins at Lake Louise\, through the east 
 Weaverville neighborhood\, up-up-up Hamburg mountain\, and through downtow
 n. Dogs: On leash\, with water and snacks\nHead Lamp or Flashlight ***Requ
 ired in Winter***\n\n**Starting Location:** We will meet at the [Lake Loui
 se Public Bathrooms](https://maps.app.goo.gl/kar8g1usVX7TvjjN8). Call the 
 organizer if you can not find us. 828-290-0886\n**If you are running late*
 *: Park at the [Presbyterian Church](https://maps.app.goo.gl/RkA7VmJJy9bFE
 cF8A) and intercept us.\n30 Alabama Ave\, Weaverville\, NC 28787\n\n**In c
 ase of bad weather\, the hike will cancel by 4:00 pm\, and be rescheduled 
 to the following week.**\n\n**Route:** [Weaverville Wander](https://www.al
 ltrails.com/explore/map/weaverville-wander-improved-c0c783b)\n\nCautions: 
 There is a 300 ft stretch along Hamburg Mountain road\, which has limited 
 shoulder and will require us to walk single-file.\n\n**Know your pace!** P
 lease note that this is a relatively fast paced hike\, 3.2 mph even up hil
 ls. On flat sections\, we will go faster. Please be aware of your abilitie
 s and level of physical fitness. We will stop and wait for people to catch
  up in certain spots and for water breaks\, but we don't want to leave peo
 ple behind or wait a long time. It will take about 2 - 3 hrs to complete.\
 n\n**Scenic Asheville Series:** There are [9 hikes in the series](https://
 docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5L
 k/edit?usp=drive_link)\; hike them all and receive an attractive badge for
  your backpack. Check your status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadshe
 ets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\nPeo
 ple who hike as guests or plus ones are not tracked on the spreadsheet.\nB
 adgers are always welcome on any hike\, even if there's a wait list.\n\n**
 On-Time Departure**\nI typically have 1 or 2 no-shows on my hikes\, so we 
 don't wait for people to arrive. If you are late\, you'll be left behind.\
 n\n*Please change your RSVP as soon as you know you can't make it.\n- Note
 s and comments are genuinely appreciated.\n*If you have questions\, call t
 he hike leader at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests**: If you bring a guest/plus o
 ne\, make sure they know what they are in for. No flip flops. If someone h
 ikes as a guest\, the hike will not count toward a badge. If your guest ca
 n't keep up\, turn back.\n\n**Waitlist**: Please note that people that com
 e to my hikes regularly may be bumped up above newcomers on the waitlist\,
  particularly if they only need 1 or 2 hikes to get their badge. This is t
 o reward people who come regularly\, and it is also to be fair to new peop
 le who want to be on the hikes. Please keep an eye on your RSVP status.\n\
 n**Disclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking o
 n city streets that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for the
 ir safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer
  and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to or
 ganize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowle
 dge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\
 , illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated w
 ith this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup
  terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316598648
 /
