SUMMARY:```Mills River: Bad Fork &\; MST – 7 miles\, 1275’ ascent
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**How to find us**: Mills River In
 gles\, 3338 Boylston Hwy\, in front of gas pumps\, closest to Boylston Hwy
 . Departing on time.\n**Directions to Mills River Ingles**: I-26 Exit on N
 C-280 West\, Airport Road---4.3 miles to the Ingles on the right.\nPretty 
 hike along a stream. Up Wash Creek Rd (FS5000) for 0.6 miles. Right on Bad
  Fork Trail for a 1.8 mile ascent with some steep sections to the BRP at B
 ent Creek Gap. Left on the Forest Service Rd\, under the BRP\, right throu
 gh a tunnel\, then right for 1 mile on the MST. Reverse course and return 
 to the BRP for a snack break\, then follow the same route back to the cars
 . Type: In-out. Max elev: 3300’. Avg moving pace: 2.4 mph. Difficulty (1
 =effortless\, 10=hard): 5.5. Dogs: welcome if well-behaved\, subject to ar
 ea restrictions.\n**Trailhead**: Wash Creek Campsite.\n**Directions to Tra
 ilhead**: From Mills River Ingles to the trailhead (6.7 miles): West (left
 ) on North Mills River Rd for 4.8 miles to Wash Creek Rd (FS5000) near the
  North Mills River Campground. Turn right onto FS5000 for 1.9 miles (mostl
 y gravel) to the first left (FS142). Park at that intersection (limited sp
 aces). Do not turn left across the concrete bridge. Please Note: There is 
 limited parking at the trailhead---please meet at Mills River Ingles for c
 ar pool to the trailhead.\n\n\\*\\*Courtesy (Please read carefully!)\\*\\*
  Only sign up if you \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\
 , please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid drop
 ping out last-minute so that wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And 
 please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316707677
 /
